{"title": "Hiring Update: Progress and Next Steps", "slides": [
  {
    "title": "Roles Open",
    "bullets": [
      "Product Manager – focused on scaling core features",
      "Frontend Engineer – to support UI/UX improvements",
      "Data Analyst – for customer behavior insights",
      "Customer Success Lead – to strengthen onboarding"
    ],
    "notes": "We’ve identified four key roles that align with our current growth priorities. Each role supports a specific area of product development and customer experience. These are the most critical hires to complete in the next quarter.",
    "layout": "bullets"
  },
  {
    "title": "Pipeline Status",
    "bullets": [
      "30+ qualified candidates in pipeline across all roles",
      "Active outreach in tech hubs and industry events",
      "Strong signals from early interviews indicating cultural fit",
      "Two roles have progressed to final rounds"
    ],
    "notes": "Our candidate pipeline is robust and shows momentum. We’re seeing consistent interest, especially in engineering and product roles. Early feedback suggests strong alignment with our team values and work style.",
    "layout": "bullets"
  },
  {
    "title": "Key Risks",
    "bullets": [
      "Delayed hiring could slow feature delivery timelines",
      "High competition in frontend and data roles",
      "Potential mismatch in remote work expectations",
      "Limited bandwidth during Q3 transition period"
    ],
    "notes": "We must act quickly to avoid bottlenecks in development and customer onboarding. The remote work expectations are particularly sensitive—ensuring clarity upfront is essential. We’re monitoring the pipeline closely to mitigate delays.",
    "layout": "bullets"
  },
  {
    "title": "Next Steps",
    "bullets": [
      "Finalize hiring decisions by end of month",
      "Onboard new hires within two weeks of offer acceptance",
      "Schedule quarterly review to assess impact on delivery timelines",
      "Share progress with leadership team biweekly"
    ],
    "notes": "We’ll move swiftly to close open roles and ensure minimal disruption. Onboarding will be structured to support rapid contribution. This cadence allows for transparency and accountability across the leadership team.",
    "layout": "bullets"
  }
]}

